The error comes from the `SELECT ... INTO` on line 4. It raises `ORA-01403: no data found` when the query returns no row. With the current `JOIN`, a department that exists but has no manager (`manager_id IS NULL`, or a manager id that does not match an employee row) produces no row, so the function fails instead of returning `NULL`.

The repair below changes the `JOIN` to a `LEFT JOIN`, so a department row with no matching manager still returns one row with `e.last_name` as `NULL`. If the department id itself does not exist, the query still returns no row and the function will still raise `ORA-01403`; if callers also expect `NULL` for unknown department ids, that is a separate business decision.

```plsql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION manager_name(p_department_id IN NUMBER) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
  l_name employees.last_name%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT e.last_name INTO l_name
    FROM departments d LEFT JOIN employees e ON e.employee_id = d.manager_id
   WHERE d.department_id = p_department_id;
  RETURN l_name;
END manager_name;
```

